arch=x86
vmlinux_btf=6.17 kernel BTF dump (bpftool btf dump file /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux format c, Ubuntu 24.04.4, 6.17.0-35-generic)
clang=Ubuntu clang version 18.1.3 (1ubuntu1)
load_verified=bpftool prog loadall, Ubuntu x86_64 7.0.0-42-generic, all 14
  programs pinned; the full provider test suite also passes there. That host has
  "bpf" in its active LSM list, so rt_open() takes the LSM dpath rung on it, and
  its struct renamedata is the 5-field layout with new_dentry at offset 32 --
  the variant the CO-RE branch resolves rather than the shadow struct's.
notes=rebuilt for P0 (mnt_want_write/write_mnt_map, resolve_dentry, dual
  renamedata layout, mount-boundary advance), the P2 ABI MINOR 2 contract
  (euid/login_uid) and the P3 LSM parity work (14 programs, three-rung
  dpath/walk/kprobe ladder). The header moved from the 6.6
  dump the previous object used to a 6.17 one, which is the portable direction
  per prebuilt/README.md: CO-RE resolves offsets against the running kernel, and
  a newer header defines the types the dual-layout rename branch needs. That
  change accounts for part of the object's growth from 1287696 bytes; the rest
  is the P2 and P3 code. Current size is recorded in the check_files manifests.
  The 4.18 (CentOS Stream 8) load verification recorded for the previous object
  has NOT been repeated for this one; only the 6.17 host above was tested.
